    "post_stream": {
      "posts": [
        {
          "id": 1937890,
          "username": "djn2",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/djn2/{size}/419774_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-12T03:54:22.157Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Hi all — I often get product lists from suppliers as .xlsx, but Shopify import wants a product CSV. I didn’t want to install a monthly importer just for a one-off draft catalog.</p>\n<p>I made a small browser-based converter:</p>\n<p>- Upload .xlsx or .xls (first sheet only)</p>\n<p>- Map Title and Price (SKU optional)</p>\n<p>- Preview 5 products free</p>\n<p>- $3 for the full CSV, Status = draft</p>\n<p>It does not connect to the store. You download the file and import it in admin. One Excel row becomes one single-variant draft product.</p>\n<p>Tool: <a href=\"https://djnsbbx.space/tools/excel-shopify/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Excel → Shopify Draft CSV — Preview Free, Full Export $3 | bbx</a></p>\n<p>If this doesn’t fit (multi-sheet workbooks, variant matrices, or live sync), the usual app route is still the better option.</p>",
          "post_number": 1,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 4,
          "updated_at": "2026-11-12T03:54:22.157Z",
