        {
          "id": 1941377,
          "username": "sabbit1",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/sabbit1/{size}/419691_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-16T07:56:44.487Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Good point from <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/badhon_rafi\">@Badhon_Rafi</a> on variants — Excel adds a few traps of its own before you even get to that. First, check which sheet is actually first: suppliers often hide the real price list behind a cover sheet, and a converter reading only the first sheet will import the wrong one. Second, watch numbers Excel has already changed — SKUs with leading zeros lose them (00123 becomes 123), and prices with currency symbols or commas arrive as text, not numbers, so sort and check the Price column before importing. Third, keep one row per variant, with the same Handle repeated, or Shopify will create separate products instead of one product with options. Import five rows as drafts first, then check the handle grouping, SKU uniqueness and option values before importing the full file.</p>",
          "post_number": 4,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 4,
          "updated_at": "2026-11-16T07:56:44.487Z",
