    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 1884854,
      "summarized_text": "A browser-based tool was shared for converting supplier Excel files (.xlsx or .xls) into Shopify product CSVs without installing an app or connecting to a store. It reads only the first worksheet, lets users map product title and price (with SKU optional), previews five products for free, and charges $3 for a full CSV marked as draft. Each spreadsheet row becomes a separate single-variant draft product, so it may not suit files containing multiple variants or requiring live synchronization.\n\nReplies highlighted practical risks and alternatives. Supplier rows for different sizes or colors should be grouped into one product using a shared Shopify handle; otherwise, Shopify may create duplicates. Matching rows by SKU and reviewing a report of matched, updated, and unmatched items can also help manage repeat imports. Before importing, check that the first worksheet is the correct one, preserve SKUs with leading zeros, and ensure prices are numeric rather than text. The recommendation is to test a small batch as drafts and verify handles, SKU uniqueness, and option values before a full import. No final decision or resolution was reported.",
